/**
 * @file src/AnalysisG/metrics/topefficiency/include/metrics/topefficiency.h
 * @brief Header file for the topefficiency selection and metric evaluation class.
 * 
 * This file defines the topefficiency class which evaluates the performance of top quark 
 * reconstruction and related machine learning inferences. It contains methods and 
 * data structures to evaluate predictions against truth information for top quarks and Z' bosons.
 * 
 * @class topefficiency
 * @brief Evaluates top quark reconstruction efficiency and kinematics.
 * 
 * This class inherits from selection_template and implements methods to evaluate
 * event strategies (`strategy`) and selections (`selection`). It supports binning
 * across transverse momentum (pt) and pseudorapidity (eta) and tracks numerous metrics
 * including top/Z' mass, decay regions, node multiplicities, and probabilities.
 * 
 * It also maintains variables necessary for ROC curve generation (truth/prediction edge
 * scores, number of tops, and signal classification).
 * 
 * Key Methods:
 * - `iters`: Helper to determine bin iterations.
 * - `region`: Classifies a pt/eta combination into a specific region.
 * - `decaymode`: Analyzes a vector of top quarks to classify their collective decay mode.
 */
